From 947451d519437ca72996a8696b729e4e8e0219ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T3chnobone <98963290+T3chnobone@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:21:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/17] Add local multiplayer for up to 8 players and
 multi-monitor views

Local Grand Prix with up to 8 human drivers on one PC (built on the netplay
"big race"), each with their own view and HUD. Each view is rendered into its
own framebuffer sized to its place on screen and composed onto the window,
which can span several monitors as one borderless window.

- Settings window: players and characters, automatic one-gamepad-per-player
  assignment, monitor selection and spanning with a layout preview, view
  render scale, window size presets.
- Per-screen state sized for 8 screens (kart animation, palettes, matrices,
  screen contexts); camera-indexed arrays sized to NUM_CAMERAS.
- Players 5-8 read from controller ports 5-8; larger per-frame gfx pools.
- Requires the matching libultraship change (8 ports, own-aspect
  framebuffers, monitor list / borderless window).

See docs/LOCAL_MULTIPLAYER.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
